WEBVTT

00:00:00.499 --> 00:00:02.733
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Tim Powell isn’t a morning person.

00:00:02.839 --> 00:00:07.288
Which is surprising, because on weekdays he gets up very early.

00:00:07.778 --> 00:00:12.472
While most of us are still asleep, Powell wakes up at 5.45,

00:00:12.655 --> 00:00:17.758
does exercise for 30 minutes in his home gym, and has a big breakfast.

00:00:18.478 --> 00:00:21.752
Then he gets ready for work and drives to the office.

00:00:22.492 --> 00:00:27.602
When he gets to the building where he works, he goes for a walk around a local park,

00:00:27.952 --> 00:00:31.419
then he goes inside to start work at 9.

00:00:31.942 --> 00:00:38.421
And on Thursdays he gets up even earlier, at 5.20 a.m., to study German.

00:00:39.291 --> 00:00:41.006
Powell is a lawyer.

00:00:41.313 --> 00:00:48.013
He works 70 hours a week, and he says that getting up early helps him to do more during the day.

00:00:48.671 --> 00:00:54.257
He isn’t the only one – many busy, successful people get up very early.